# Beat (week 5, Monday) — the sibling almost says something real, then
# deflects; the friend the player has never heard of. cast.md § 3.2: "A
# moment where they almost say something real, then deflect"; "The brief
# mention of a friend the player has never heard of."
# TODO: authenticity check — "Jess" is a placeholder.

Late. {GameState.sibling_name} is sitting on the back steps when you take the trash out. He moves over to make room. You sit.
"Do you ever think about—" He stops. Laughs at nothing. "Never mind. It's dumb."
"Jess says I overthink everything."
- "Who's Jess?"
	[signal arg="EXPOSE:1.5"]
	[signal arg="BUMP:sibling_close"]
	[signal arg="FLAG:asked_about_jess"]
	"Nobody. A friend." He stands. "From work. You'd like her, actually." He says it like he's testing a floorboard with one foot. "Night."
- "Think about what?"
	"Nothing. Forget it." He bumps your shoulder with his. "You're gonna be an elder someday, you know that? You've got the face for it."
You sit on the step a while after he goes in. The motion light over the garage clicks off.
